<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  fleet-pin-watch — report pinned worktrees that stopped receiving merged work.

  THIS UNIT ARMS NOTHING, two ways. It passes the pins-only flag, which checks pins and
  returns before cycle() is reached at all; and FLEET_WATCH_REPOS is deliberately
  ABSENT, so even without that flag cycle() warns "nothing to scan" and returns 0
  before any lease, spawn or spend.
  That flag also keeps this out of the dispatch watcher's cycle lock, which it
  would otherwise hold across two network fetches. That is the watcher's own rule — an unconfigured
  allowlist dispatches nothing — used on purpose here. Verified before shipping by
  running the watcher in dry-run with FLEET_WATCH_REPOS unset and FLEET_PINS set:
      -> "FLEET_WATCH_REPOS is empty — nothing to scan" / "0 would dispatch"
  If you ever add FLEET_WATCH_REPOS to THIS unit you have armed plan dispatch on
  a 30-minute timer. Don't; give dispatch its own unit and its own decision.

  It runs from the PINNED eunomia worktree, not ~/dev/eunomia. fleet-collect and
  fleet-leak-watch were installed from the shared clone until 2026-09-07 and so
  executed whatever branch a session last left checked out — the exact defect
  this check exists to report. Both are installed from the pin now. The repo
  copies were themselves wrong until 2026-09-07 and were deployed the same day,
  so the gap here was never repo-vs-deployment — it was that nothing reported
  either half, which is what this unit is for. The checker therefore also checks its OWN pin: a fix to it does not
  reach this unit until someone re-points, and until then the check says so.

  Install (opshost) — AFTER the pin carries a fleet-watch that has check_pins,
  or this runs and reports nothing while looking installed:
    (advance the pin first — docs/secret-guard.md owns the fetch-and-detach
     procedure; a second copy here is the drift risk this repo keeps finding)
    grep -c 'def check_pins' ~/.local/share/pins/eunomia/bin/fleet-watch   # must be 1
    cp launchd/org.eunomia.fleet-pin-watch.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.eunomia.fleet-pin-watch.plist

  Verify per PROVENANCE 8.3 — see it report before trusting it: move a pin
  backwards — check it out one commit back, detached — and confirm the next run
  logs `pin stale:`. Then put it back. Ordering trap: check_pins is
  transition-gated, so a pin already recorded stale stays silent. Bring it
  current, let one cycle record that, and only then move it back.

  DO NOT also expect a PUSH on that same run (plan 0059). A pin moved back one
  commit is still fast-forwardable, so fleet-pin-advance would heal it
  unaided, and check_pins now delays a page for exactly that case until its
  StartInterval plus a margin has passed with nothing having healed it. The
  `pin stale:` log line is the proof this unit ran and saw the drift; no push
  on that same run is expected behaviour here, not a defect.

  30 minutes, not 2: a pin changes when a human merges and re-points, and each
  cycle fetches once per pin.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>org.eunomia.fleet-pin-watch</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/operator/.local/share/pins/eunomia/bin/fleet-watch</string>
    <string>--pins-only</string>
  </array>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>FLEET_PINS</key>
    <string>/Users/operator/.local/share/pins/eunomia,/Users/operator/.local/share/pins/techne</string>
    <!-- replace with the real Fleet-ops push URL at install; empty = log-only -->
    <key>FLEET_NTFY_URL</key><string></string>
    <!-- FLEET_WATCH_REPOS is ABSENT ON PURPOSE. See the comment above. -->
  </dict>
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>1800</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>ProcessType</key><string>Background</string>
  <key>LowPriorityIO</key><true/>
  <key>Nice</key><integer>5</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/operator/dev/.fleet/pin-watch.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/operator/dev/.fleet/pin-watch.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
